    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406-a1">

                <pb facs="0717" n="581" xml:id="pg581"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Governor of French Guiana</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Siadoies</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Vice Consul</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Brown</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cayenne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-30">July 30, 1929</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Consul</hi>: In answer to your letter of April 9,
                    1929, I have to inform you that I have just granted to a seaplane of the Pan
                    American Airway a permit to fly over and land at Cayenne on the study trip the
                    crew of that craft is taking to South America.</p>
                <p>I shall look into the application for flight over and landing in Guiana that may
                    be sent to me by the fliers of the United States of America for study trips in a
                    friendly spirit.</p>
                <p>Be pleased [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Siadoies</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
